{
	title: 'Scrollable web tab strip',
	spec: 'The web tab strip fills the space between fixed left and right controls. When numbered tabs overflow, those controls scroll the strip without selecting a tab. Scroll controls are secondary to native horizontal touch scrolling: they are 24px wide and retain at least 44px height; numbered tab targets retain at least 44px width and height. Keep their space at either end, disabled and at 50% opacity. Page smoothly by one visible page minus one tab: the rightmost fully visible tab becomes the leftmost on a rightward page, reversed leftward, clamped at the ends. Use native momentum touch scrolling with CSS proximity scroll snap. Respect reduced motion for programmatic scrolling. Swiping never changes the active session and does not pan the page. Tapping any tab number smoothly centers that tab where possible, including tapping the already selected tab. Changing selection by other means also smoothly centers it. Respect reduced motion with immediate positioning instead. Status updates never reposition the strip. An offscreen active tab makes its corresponding chevron bold and green, with no underline, dot, or visible tab number. Controls display arrows and optional urgent status markers, never numbers that could be mistaken for tab selectors. Accessible labels report hidden counts, the most urgent hidden status and whether the active tab lies there. Named tabs still appear when they all fit. Terminal paging is unchanged. Restore the invariant that scrolling navigation never changes session selection. Browser coverage verifies overlap, centering, ends, offscreen active indicators and status-update stability.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'The strip uses overflow:hidden with CSS scroll snap: native programmatic scrolling works, but horizontal finger panning is unavailable. Cell widths expand to consume leftover space. Browser assertions await scrollend; checking visible indices during smooth animation falsely reports overlap/stability failures. Selection centers on the nearest snap boundary, so with an even visible count its position is within half a tab of exact center.',
		'User feedback: visible hidden counts looked like session numbers and made scroll controls look like tabs. Counts belong only in accessible labels; visible controls use arrows and optional status markers. Use real host state transitions for the status-update browser fixture so later normal tab publications cannot overwrite a synthetic failed state.',
		'Solid effect sources compare values by identity. Returning a fresh array of selection/layout inputs recentered the strip on status redraws; use a stable scalar key so unchanged selection and geometry do not run the centering effect.',
		'The decisive status-update fix is stable DOM identity: key strip links by session id, not incoming Tab objects. Status broadcasts replace those objects; recreating the snapped link makes the browser reset scroll. Preserve links and guard the centering key explicitly.',
		'Selection centering uses native smooth scrollTo, not Solid transitions. Strip links also recenter on a plain click, so tapping the already selected tab recenters after manual paging. The browser test awaits native scrollend before checking the final centered position.',
		'Supersedes the no-swipe choice: native overflow-x:auto and proximity snapping provide momentum without custom gesture code. Secondary chevrons are 24px wide by at least 44px tall; offscreen active direction is bold green only. Real Chrome touch-drag coverage verifies strip movement does not change session selection. Momentum can end before touchEnd, so the test waits for stable position rather than subscribing to scrollend after the gesture.',
		'Bug fix invariant: an edge marks hidden tabs only when tabs actually lie beyond it; at the scroll end the right edge is empty. The visible range uses rendered width (scrollWidth / tab count), since the computed cell drifts from layout-unit rounding across 100+ tabs, and the scroll end counts as the last tab visible. Seen on iOS Safari at tab 124 as a green chevron with a marker.',
		'User feedback: an edge must not repeat a marker still visible on its tab. Edge marks come only from tabs under 10% visible, both directions; counts, paging and the active-tab highlight still use fully visible tabs.'
	],
	needs: ['3k'],
	foldInto: ['3k']
